{
  "an5.33:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 5.33 ",
  "an5.33:0.2": "4. With Sumanā ",
  "an5.33:0.3": "With Uggaha ",
  "an5.33:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Bhaddiya in Jātiyā Wood. ",
  "an5.33:1.2": "Then Uggaha, Meṇḍaka’s grandson, went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him, ",
  "an5.33:2.1": "“Sir, would the Buddha, together with three other monks, please accept tomorrow’s meal from me?” ",
  "an5.33:2.2": "The Buddha consented with silence. ",
  "an5.33:2.3": "Then, knowing that the Buddha had consented, Uggaha rose from his seat, bowed, and respectfully circled the Buddha, keeping him on his right, before leaving. ",
  "an5.33:3.1": "Then when the night had passed, the Buddha robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, went to Uggaha’s home, where he sat down on the seat spread out. ",
  "an5.33:3.2": "Then Uggaha served and satisfied the Buddha with his own hands with delicious fresh and cooked foods. ",
  "an5.33:3.3": "When the Buddha had eaten and washed his hand and bowl, Uggaha sat down to one side, ",
  "an5.33:3.4": "and said to him, ",
  "an5.33:3.5": "“Sir, these girls of mine will be going to their husbands’ families. ",
  "an5.33:3.6": "May the Buddha please advise ",
  "an5.33:3.7": "and instruct them. It will be for their lasting welfare and happiness.” ",
  "an5.33:4.1": "Then the Buddha said to those girls: ",
  "an5.33:4.2": "“So, girls, you should train like this: ",
  "an5.33:4.3": "‘Our parents will give us t